[{:db/id "q-32818/selection/1bfde53ac82644e21099b72df26dcc087899ef649cb30159cc64523890c85587" :answer/id #uuid "84f3e9f8-8af0-5a19-b3fe-fc9c0ea0f5f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=3t \\\\ y=6t \\\\ z=8t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32818/selection/ef10d5b49560bce9a4305ce8458ae0df35752026d320dd7fc60f9f1691275a83" :answer/id #uuid "5414db53-6619-56bb-8449-68daf5d5bc2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-5t \\\\ y=-11t \\\\ z=-4t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32818/selection/0debf42ee5471be1344721f7fe6a6832b497bef5e21d7b1e86446b30db3d0ad5" :answer/id #uuid "51ccc64f-ba35-50df-9939-e2a12ff85188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+3t \\\\ y=-11+6t \\\\ z=-4+8t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32818/selection/88a356d0f1d005d8b1ff77a4e89ad6042ca4d790e38e11bb2aa0a34cc35fecd2" :answer/id #uuid "fc9d07b8-653d-5448-9865-94f13110407e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2+3t \\\\ y=-5+6t \\\\ z=4+8t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32818/selection/77fa612cb4b22c9ff5df8eac12c966e63621030d424d3b37226ca245a7b40e37" :answer/id #uuid "8f95886e-0710-5d17-9e90-55fc7b4dee02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32818/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4140aab5-f5b9-5b71-bde7-b995e7150c80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32818/selection/77fa612cb4b22c9ff5df8eac12c966e63621030d424d3b37226ca245a7b40e37" :answer-field/choices ["q-32818/selection/1bfde53ac82644e21099b72df26dcc087899ef649cb30159cc64523890c85587" "q-32818/selection/ef10d5b49560bce9a4305ce8458ae0df35752026d320dd7fc60f9f1691275a83" "q-32818/selection/0debf42ee5471be1344721f7fe6a6832b497bef5e21d7b1e86446b30db3d0ad5" "q-32818/selection/88a356d0f1d005d8b1ff77a4e89ad6042ca4d790e38e11bb2aa0a34cc35fecd2" "q-32818/selection/77fa612cb4b22c9ff5df8eac12c966e63621030d424d3b37226ca245a7b40e37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32818" :question/id #uuid "3e0ace14-c4d0-53ea-821e-4f626073eb45" :question/math-academy-id "q-32818" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/assets/99504eaa41497c5be9baa7c860c97ab5ba5c858609e47ad347f24ec9b8ffc940.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,6,8)$ and $Q(-2,-5,4).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5t \\\\ -11t \\\\ -4t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-5t \\\\ 6-11t \\\\ 8-4t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32818/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32818"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186124866 :question/answer-fields 17592186122218] {:db/id "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/684dfe703ee9e6da5cf59233add1d762f1a3abade6d133eec98044d2b59e3173" :answer/id #uuid "26149efd-6258-5c6d-899b-8b76bd92f6a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/07a048ebe07b5cfced7695ff4b5ee215e161ddcec55f96d4e771d799532dc04d" :answer/id #uuid "c7131830-fa04-52c9-8165-83976213e7df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4+t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=2-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/01a55f739acb0a2aa80df9497b9f343aaa16c1db8052bc3e6da72858b0b3b370" :answer/id #uuid "2b80a7c1-1043-53df-9937-1c302aea271a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/8a27cb32bc7153579b0f72309cb58765f89d595b1f99da5e9ebd6813d6ca4efa" :answer/id #uuid "a1bd0392-0d4d-5e20-af94-0f8eea17c8ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=5+t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/d4ebd407657262aa00e6c3bcd37dbba7e657680907d256e35e4eb4e32709d168" :answer/id #uuid "31cb1ef6-a234-5bb7-b23d-06c409656e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-t \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a7ef8f-c4b6-5c5b-9714-eade580df09e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/01a55f739acb0a2aa80df9497b9f343aaa16c1db8052bc3e6da72858b0b3b370" :answer-field/choices ["q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/684dfe703ee9e6da5cf59233add1d762f1a3abade6d133eec98044d2b59e3173" "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/07a048ebe07b5cfced7695ff4b5ee215e161ddcec55f96d4e771d799532dc04d" "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/01a55f739acb0a2aa80df9497b9f343aaa16c1db8052bc3e6da72858b0b3b370" "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/8a27cb32bc7153579b0f72309cb58765f89d595b1f99da5e9ebd6813d6ca4efa" "q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d/d4ebd407657262aa00e6c3bcd37dbba7e657680907d256e35e4eb4e32709d168"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36026"] :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36026/selection/ma-v1/f8ab12f0a18645b2eb2c1178e9847237aaed983816b6846db4f80d32a065dc3d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-70722/selection/3bcb3050bf112e8901822b38b8336717e0ec8a63a62b43de8fa02a9e5a00c560" :answer/id #uuid "43563c92-436c-5119-9cdc-0d2a1ad58c38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70722/selection/0b46337c2187d23d6087d952716e062f9c9c2af65ee5c299eed9a23664a67137" :answer/id #uuid "f82d71d4-c76a-5493-8fe9-fe5cdb5c703c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70722/selection/37736a8ff1c4d0ebce1c5a8aedfa8b88927825d4f5edda71672553fd75facbe2" :answer/id #uuid "b1599866-bc5c-5705-82d6-f8df38ef492f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70722/selection/00b7b3512880ffd2190b437057f7e62bf69263980a6fea56b5864e100283ec80" :answer/id #uuid "37269206-ff38-5158-a69f-5bf7c914f100" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70722/selection/c09b402d9397773724cb0f62353022eb11c89db7f9f4aefc6c00023cddf65d04" :answer/id #uuid "c6e16bed-11d8-56fc-9786-9b35848e825a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70722/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "970e7078-7224-55a4-b236-058de0e89bbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70722/selection/00b7b3512880ffd2190b437057f7e62bf69263980a6fea56b5864e100283ec80" :answer-field/choices ["q-70722/selection/3bcb3050bf112e8901822b38b8336717e0ec8a63a62b43de8fa02a9e5a00c560" "q-70722/selection/0b46337c2187d23d6087d952716e062f9c9c2af65ee5c299eed9a23664a67137" "q-70722/selection/37736a8ff1c4d0ebce1c5a8aedfa8b88927825d4f5edda71672553fd75facbe2" "q-70722/selection/00b7b3512880ffd2190b437057f7e62bf69263980a6fea56b5864e100283ec80" "q-70722/selection/c09b402d9397773724cb0f62353022eb11c89db7f9f4aefc6c00023cddf65d04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70722" :question/id #uuid "b555bc5f-ed8b-573d-be10-fd205e56f99f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70722" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ y=5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ 5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(1,5,\\frac{1}{3})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70722/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-236389/field-1/5d2f716a33503eec53ec624986c4300a233a9102d878bf79ff6824e1dcb44066" :answer/id #uuid "a73fe140-3a26-5c33-b76d-7182da90c8b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236389/field-1/644fbe1bba16091ac89b998dd381e22e789a6b1b974026b768886108b4568886" :answer/id #uuid "979248b0-67ce-5295-b739-98d0f9c9a5dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121555 :answer-field/correct "q-236389/field-1/5d2f716a33503eec53ec624986c4300a233a9102d878bf79ff6824e1dcb44066" :answer-field/choices ["q-236389/field-1/5d2f716a33503eec53ec624986c4300a233a9102d878bf79ff6824e1dcb44066" "q-236389/field-1/644fbe1bba16091ac89b998dd381e22e789a6b1b974026b768886108b4568886"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236389/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9daa492b-2b2f-5a2a-870c-36a8804a3e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121557 :answer-field/correct "q-236389/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-236389/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236389/field-3/20aaaf6f8c81dddeb0440d212d067c75496bcd1f11c7aea53087cdcb4f03f1bc" :answer/id #uuid "e8caaea8-b523-5b0a-9fd8-80d04d8092a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2+3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121556 :answer-field/correct "q-236389/field-3/20aaaf6f8c81dddeb0440d212d067c75496bcd1f11c7aea53087cdcb4f03f1bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-236389/field-3/20aaaf6f8c81dddeb0440d212d067c75496bcd1f11c7aea53087cdcb4f03f1bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-236389"] :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(-2,3,1).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-2}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $4-t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ -t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-3t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-236986/field-1/678f257b1f54a82e5db486492f5f9ca40e9d8c374eced28c7481ae3fd8d856c0" :answer/id #uuid "2a3199e0-7ca6-5317-9afa-2d99c3b3771e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5+t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121558 :answer-field/correct "q-236986/field-1/678f257b1f54a82e5db486492f5f9ca40e9d8c374eced28c7481ae3fd8d856c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-236986/field-1/678f257b1f54a82e5db486492f5f9ca40e9d8c374eced28c7481ae3fd8d856c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236986/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "58069a6a-b603-54fd-bc70-e51cd1dd4dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121559 :answer-field/correct "q-236986/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-236986/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-236986"] :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-5,7,1)$ and $Q(-4,-1,6).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [$ {{field-2}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $7-8t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | $1+5t$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -8t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5+t \\\\ 7-8t \\\\ 1+5t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+t \\\\ y=7-8t \\\\ z=1+5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
